# Phase 14 — Final Acceptance Tests

The implementation is **not complete** until these scenarios work.

### Successful request

```text
User → "Show my alerts"

Debug:

✓ Request
✓ Intent
✓ Agent
✓ API
✓ Data
✓ Context
✓ Ollama request
✓ Ollama response
✓ Parser
✓ Final response
```

### Backend failure

```text
User → "Show my alerts"

Debug:

✓ Request
✓ Intent
✓ Agent
✗ API → 500

Error:
DatabaseError
Endpoint:
/api/alerts
Request ID:
REQ-A81F42
```

### Ollama failure

```text
✓ API
✓ Data
✓ Context
✗ Ollama → timeout
```

### Frontend parsing failure

```text
✓ Ollama
✗ Response Parser
```

### Debug infrastructure test

The artificial debug test must visibly stream:

```text
Event 1
   ↓
Event 2
   ↓
Event 3
   ↓
Event 4
   ↓
Event 5
```

**without refreshing the page.**

---

## Commit Strategy

Do this as separate commits and **test each commit before moving forward**:

```text
1. audit-current-ai-flow
2. add-request-trace-id
3. add-debug-event-contract
4. instrument-django-ai-flow
5. instrument-ml-ollama-flow
6. fix-structured-error-propagation
7. add-sse-or-websocket-debug-stream
8. add-debug-stream-test-endpoint
9. add-debug-failure-scenarios
10. build-live-debug-pipeline-ui
11. connect-real-events-to-debug-ui
12. expose-ollama-context-and-response
13. fix-insights-report-alert-flows
14. fix-goal-budget-explain-flows
15. fix-chat-rendering
16. auto-execute-ai-capabilities
17. add-end-to-end-ai-tests
18. final-debug-mode-cleanup
```

### Hard requirement

**Do not mark a commit complete just because the code compiles or the UI appears.**

For every commit, actually run the relevant API/test and verify the expected behavior.

The most important milestone is **Commit 8**: the artificial debug-stream test must prove that the frontend can receive multiple backend events in real time. If that does not work, **stop there and fix the transport before touching the AI agents**.

This separates the problem into two independently testable systems:

```text
DEBUG INFRASTRUCTURE
        +
ACTUAL AI PIPELINE
```

Once the infrastructure itself is proven to work, we can reliably diagnose why `/report`, `/insights`, etc. are failing instead of repeatedly changing the UI and hoping the problem disappears.
